<header class="page-heading"><div class="eyebrow">05 / About</div><h1>The person<br>walking around.</h1></header><section class="about-layout"><div><p>I’m Aditya Singh. I have moved from software engineering into marketing, and I am currently pursuing an MBA in Marketing at NMIMS Mumbai.</p><p>ThinkInPark is a place to make that overlap visible: brands and systems, data and behaviour, technology and the much messier business of people deciding what matters to them.</p><p>I am especially interested in the work of making complex things understandable without making them dull. This is where I leave the observations, questions, and small projects that grow out of that interest.</p></div><aside class="about-aside"><section><div class="eyebrow">Currently</div><p>Exploring startup use cases in India, customer trust in financial products, and the shape of good positioning.</p></section><section><div class="eyebrow">Elsewhere</div><p><a href="contact.html">Say hello →</a></p></section><section><div class="eyebrow">On paper</div><p>The short, formal version of all this. <button class="button button--quiet" id="resume-toggle-about" data-resume-trigger>Résumé</button></p></section><section><div class="eyebrow">Between walks</div><p>I also point a camera at things that catch my eye. <a href="photographs.html">A few frames →</a></p></section></aside></section>
